# GitHub account-specific SSH aliases.
#
# 1. Choose connection variant
#    - Local-key
#    - Proxy
#    - JumpHost proxy
# 2. Replace github.com-myuser with a short account alias.
# 3. If you use agent forwarding, keep IdentitiesOnly no and
#      omit IdentityFile.
# 4. If you keep the key on this machine, set IdentityFile and
#      use IdentitiesOnly yes.
# 5. Point repository remotes at the alias, for example:
#      git remote set-url origin git@github.com-myuser:OWNER/REPO.git

# 1. Local-key variant:
#
# Host github.com-myuser-local
#   HostName github.com
#   User git
#   IdentitiesOnly yes
#   IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_myuser

# 2. Proxy variant:
#
# Host github.com-myuser
#   HostName github.com
#   User git
#   IdentitiesOnly no
#   ProxyCommand nc -X connect -x proxy.example.com:PORT %h %p

# 3. JumpHost proxy variant:
#
# Host JumpHost
#   User user
#   HostName ip-address
#   ForwardAgent yes
#
# Host github.com-myuser
#   HostName github.com
#   User git
#   IdentitiesOnly no
#   ProxyCommand ssh -q JumpHost nc -X connect -x proxy.example.com:PORT %h %p
